==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|rectum}}, abbreviation of {{der|en|la||rectum intestinum|the straight intestine}}, {{m|la|rectum}}, neuter of {{m|la|rectus||straight}}. See {{m|en|right}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛktəm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-rectum.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|recta|rectums}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[terminal]] part of the large [[intestine]] through which [[feces]] pass.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|rectal}}

